      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e44a1bd0c91c2477a8b8acb|full_name}: unfortunatly that just cutsoff and resets it rather than stops it. with that instead of worrying about constantly touching the trigger to keep it at 0 until actually pressed, the NotEqual1 now cuts it off a resets it when you do intend to press trigger full so you have to be careful not to press trigger pull.",
